# 13–14px Desktop Baseline & 0.9em Code

The fundamental purpose of typography in productivity software is to sustain high-density, low-fatigue information intake across hours of continuous work.

## Productivity Tools vs Marketing Pages

- **Marketing Sites / Blogs**: Prefer larger type (16px–20px) with loose leading to capture passive attention and encourage rapid scrolling.
- **Desktop Productivity Tools (IDEs, Consoles, CoreBox)**: Must anchor body type between 13px–14px. Oversized type dilutes information density, forcing constant eye travel that violates the Gestalt Law of Proximity and accelerates visual exhaustion.

## The 13–14px Optical Scanning Baseline

The human foveal vision window covers approximately 2 degrees. At typical desktop viewing distances (50cm–70cm), 13px–14px allows full word units to land inside the fovea, optimizing scanning velocity:

- **Controls & Data Rows (13px–14px)**: Input field values, table cells, button labels.
- **Secondary Copy (12px)**: Helper copy, empty state notes, shortcut badges.
- **Micro-labels (10px–11px)**: All-caps tags or miniature badges.
- **Headings (15px–18px)**: Reserved strictly for card and module titles; prose never exceeds 14px.
- **Display numerals (22px–32px)**: Stat cards, chart summaries and metric values.

